B.aV4=new A.ar("Two paths. Clipper on this device copies a LinkedIn profile into Orgora (nothing is sent to us). Orgora on Grok can also help find a profile URL you confirm and a public headshot \u2014 that writes through Connect into your Drive or OneDrive, not through Clipper.\n\nClipper: on the photo, tap Orgora (or Clip to Orgora in the corner). Waiting clips show on the Home Import from LinkedIn tile as a blue Review N row. Account \u2192 Import from LinkedIn opens that inbox on iPhone, Mac, and web. Chrome on the computer opens Orgora with the person ready to import \u2014 it does not download a file. The profile photo from that clip shows on the person's card. When there is no photo, the card shows initials. On iPhone and iPad, Open LinkedIn and a profile link open Safari, not the LinkedIn app, so the extension can run.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.aFF=s([B.aV4,B.aA,B.uQ],t.p)
B.Um=new A.tP(B.aR,B.L,B.Q,B.aw,null,B.dt,null,0,B.aFF,null)
B.b_a=new A.h5(B.pE,"Import from LinkedIn",B.Um,null)
B.XJ=new A.bj(61563,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.aVs=new A.ar("Orgora Charts maps people, reporting lines, products, and use cases. You sign in with Google or Microsoft \u2014 that SSO is your Orgora account. Sign-in is sync: charts live in your Google Drive or OneDrive across web, iPhone, and Mac. There is no separate backup product \u2014 sign-in already syncs.\n\nAfter sign-in, Home lists your cloud charts plus the sample, the Grok Bot tile, and LinkedIn tools. Search is in the bar. Tap your photo for account: Import contacts, Products, LinkedIn, Submit a ticket, Help, Backup Drive, then Sign out at the bottom. Delete account is under Help \u2192 Privacy \u2014 it removes Orgora Charts files from that Drive or OneDrive and this device; it does not delete your Google or Microsoft account. The Grok Bot tile and Import contacts \u2192 Ask Grok Bot open the Orgora Charts Bot template. Backup Drive is an optional second Google account that receives a replica of each chart \u2014 not a sign-in. A ticket includes your sign-in email. If saving to Drive or OneDrive does not finish, Sign out anyway still leaves this device. The charts stay in your cloud.\n\nOpen the sample chart to look around first. The sample counts toward the free-tier chart limit (three charts including the sample).",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_b=new A.h5(B.XJ,"Getting started",B.aVs,null)
B.aW2=new A.ar("Open a chart, then Share (not the account avatar menu). Send a PDF picture, an Orgora file the other person opens in Orgora Charts, or Share with email (Google Drive / OneDrive).\n\nEmail share: they open the Drive/OneDrive file with Orgora (from the share email \u2014 sign-in alone is not enough on Google Drive), then it is added when they have room under the free chart total \u2014 or Pro. A shared Orgora file snapshot stays free to view; saving an editable copy from that file still follows the free-tier size limits unless they are Pro.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_c=new A.h5(B.py,"Sharing a chart",B.aW2,null)
B.aVB=new A.ar("On Home, the Grok Bot tile shows create, connected, or update: tap Orgora Charts on Grok Bot to create, or Update your Grok Bot when the template has a newer version (Ask Grok Bot under Import contacts opens the same template). Connect Orgora with the same Google or Microsoft account \u2014 that writes charts into your Drive or OneDrive so iPhone, Mac, and web stay aligned. After Connect, Orgora stays signed in with a refresh token so you should not need to re-auth every hour. Mail and screenshots stay in Grok; Orgora does not take mailbox passwords. The Bot can also pull company logos, help confirm LinkedIn profiles, attach headshots when a public photo URL is available (LinkedIn often blocks cloud page scrapes \u2014 the Bot uses the photo URL from search, or you can use the Clipper), and refresh Warm/Hot/Cold from mail activity (same forward-only rules as Connect mailbox on this device \u2014 on demand or when you ask to refresh lead status).\n\nThe Bot template is listed with xAI \u2014 you do not need a separate MCP menu item in Orgora to use it.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_d=new A.h5(B.pF,"Connectors",B.aVB,null)
B.aWm=new A.ar("Each chart is its own org. Search by name or website, star favorites, and tap New org chart under the list. A chart's menu can rename it, edit the company logo and website, or delete it. The name on the chart itself also renames it. Sign-in already saves the chart.\n\nCharts for your signed-in account load on Home automatically (sign-in is sync \u2014 no Drive picker and no separate backup product). Share a chart from inside it \u2014 not from home. You can send a PDF, or an Orgora file the other person opens in the app.\n\nInside a chart: tap a person to edit them. Drag a card to change who they report to. Drag empty space to move around the chart, and scroll or pinch to zoom. The Contacts button opens a list on the left and hides again so the chart keeps the width. To park someone in that list without deleting them: tap the person-remove icon on their card, choose Move to Contacts from the \u22ee menu or a right-click / long-press, use Move to Contacts on their edit sheet, or drop their card on Contacts (open or the collapsed chip). On iPhone and Mac the list can also show people your email already found at this company.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_e=new A.h5(B.kB,"Charts",B.aWm,null)
B.aWq=new A.ar("Optional and separate from sign-in. Your Orgora account is Google or Microsoft SSO \u2014 Import contacts does not create the account.\n\nTap your photo \u2192 Import contacts. Choose:\n\n\u2022 Ask Grok Bot \u2014 opens the Orgora Charts Bot template. If Grok already has your mail, Connect Orgora there and ask for a chart from people you\u2019ve spoken with. Charts land in your Drive or OneDrive. Home also shows the same Bot tile.\n\u2022 Connect mailbox on this device \u2014 iPhone and Mac only (not in the web app). Microsoft, Gmail (app password), or Advanced (iCloud, Yahoo, IMAP). Find people scans companies in your mail and can create an org chart from a domain.\n\nDevice mailbox credentials stay in the keychain; mail is read directly from your provider. Disconnecting removes that mailbox from this device; it does not sign you out of Orgora. People you add to a chart still sync with sign-in.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_f=new A.h5(B.eT,"Import contacts",B.aWq,null)
B.aVA=new A.ar("Add someone from the chart, import contacts (tap your photo \u2192 Import contacts \u2014 Grok Bot or this device\u2019s mailbox), or clip a LinkedIn profile from the blue Home Import from LinkedIn tile. Tag a role on the person: Economic Buyer, Champion, Coach, Stakeholder, Technical, Influencer, or Gatekeeper.\n\nWaiting clips show on that tile as a blue Review N row with the name. Account \u2192 Import from LinkedIn opens the same inbox on iPhone, Mac, and web.\n\nFind people lives inside Import contacts (Find people \u2014 create charts from companies) \u2014 not on Home. It scans your own mail for work addresses and can create an org chart from that domain. Personal mail domains are grouped separately and are never suggested as a company chart.\n\nInbox imports stay off the tree. Contacts opens on the left when people still need a place (and when you take someone off the chart). Search by name, title, or email. Drag onto the chart or tap Place. Drop on a person to make them a report, or on empty canvas for a top-level seat. Anyone you leave in the list stays off the hierarchy.\n\nPerson cards use a thick border in the role color (Economic Buyer blue, Champion gold, Gatekeeper red, and so on) plus a matching chip. Warm/Cold and product tags stay beside it. The detail card also shows email and phone. Optional Hyperscalers on the People toolbar tag the organization with AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex, Azure Foundry, or Marketplace private offer. Undo and Redo are labelled next to that control.\n\nDrag a card to move that person under a new manager. Drag empty space to pan, and scroll or pinch to zoom.\n\nAdvanced: MEDDPICC one-pager (People toolbar, person \u22ee menu, or under their profile) builds a single page from this org \u2014 Economic Buyer, Champion, Gatekeeper, use-case pain and outcome, products, and Hyperscalers. The list on that page shows what is already on the chart. An empty letter says Open. That is not a score. Share as PDF.\n\nAdvanced: Salesforce (beta) under a saved person's profile links that Contact, Lead, or Account. Charts stay in Drive or OneDrive. Copy the web link into a Salesforce custom button to open the matching Orgora chart in the browser. Not an AppExchange package.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_g=new A.h5(B.wO,"People",B.aVA,null)
B.aW6=new A.ar("Create products (the software you sell) and use cases (the pains and outcomes that matter). Write pain and outcome in plain words. Tag them onto people. Each use case lists those people by name.\n\nOptional document links on a use case point at proposals, quotes, or other files you already keep in Google Drive or OneDrive \u2014 Orgora stores the link, not the file.\n\nOrgora on Grok can also create use cases from email or Granola notes, tag the right people, and attach those Drive links when you share them.\n\nWhen a use case is linked to a product, the person card shows them on one row: product on the left, use case on the right. Unlinked tags get their own line. Detail view lists every tag \u2014 nothing is hidden behind a +N chip.\n\nProducts can live on one chart or in a device-wide catalog (tap your photo \u2192 Products) so the same product appears in every org you map.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_h=new A.h5(B.pD,"Products and use cases",B.aW6,null)
B.XE=new A.bj(61284,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.aVm=new A.ar("Sign-in is sync. After you continue with Google or Microsoft, your charts live in that Google Drive or OneDrive and stay synced across web, iPhone, and Mac. There is no separate backup product \u2014 sign-in already syncs. Each chart is one Orgora file in your account \u2014 not Pro and not a public link. There is no Orgora server. Google and Microsoft own the permission list; leave every item on, then Continue. If Drive or OneDrive is skipped, Orgora asks once more. Mail is a separate, optional step \u2014 not this login.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.b_i=new A.h5(B.XE,"Save a chart",B.aVm,null)
